# HEE-v3 interface map at b5367bc (2026-10-01, louranicas-2c)
Measured from the code with `git show` / `git grep` at b5367bc, plus a read-only host check at 2026-10-01 ~06:40. Every row cites its owning module and file:line.

## 1 Unix sockets
| Socket | Owner | Role | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/habitat-engine/control.sock` | app::control_socket | the engine's only listener: control-v1 API server | `control_socket.rs:50,52,299-301` (bind); dir 0700, socket 0600 (`:146,:242,:303`); idle 60 s, write 10 s (`:57-59`) |
| `…/habitat-engine/control.lock` | app::control_socket | single-instance custody (exclusive non-blocking flock) | `control_socket.rs:54,246` |
| client connect to control.sock | main (CLI client) | `habitat-engine <action>` sends one frame and prints the reply | `main.rs:1147,1175` |
| liveness probe connect | app::control_socket | detects a live engine before replacing a stale socket | `control_socket.rs:217,278` |
No other Unix socket is bound or connected in src. The bash wrapper and Pi reach the socket only through the `habitat-engine` binary (`integrations/bash/hee3:155` producer).

## 2 Control API (control-v1 over the socket): 21 actions, 9 served, 12 refused by name
Protocol `hee3.control` (`contracts/control.rs:29`), frame ≤ 1 MiB (`:23`), version 1 only (refusal `:1235-1241`); catalogue `actions.rs:332,568`; dispatch `actions/control.rs:469-564`.
| Action | Served? | Owner / handler |
|---|---|---|
| health | yes | actions/control dispatch |
| tools.list, tools.inspect | yes | actions (catalogue) |
| task.preview | yes | app::tasks → app::routing → route (`tasks.rs:914`) |
| task.submit, task.get, task.list, task.cancel, task.resolve | yes | app::tasks StoreTasks (`tasks.rs:571-899`) → store |
| thread.get, thread.list | no (cohort, C06) | `actions/control.rs:421,425` |
| roster.list, roster.inspect, roster.update, roster.disable | no (roster, C01) | `:428-440` |
| service.inspect, service.probe, service.action | no (service, C02/C03) | `:444-452` |
| analysis.request, analysis.get | no (numerical, C04) | `:460,464` |
| events.subscribe | no (notify, B20) | `:457` |

## 3 Command-line entry points
| Entry | Owner | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `habitat-engine serve` / `serve --until-stdin-closes` | main → app (coordinator, control_socket, dispatcher) | `main.rs:261-266` |
| `habitat-engine commission <seconds>` | main → app::coordinator | `main.rs:267` |
| `habitat-engine <action> [args]` | main CLI client → control.sock | `main.rs:270, 1147` |
| `hee3 <action> …`, `hee3 --check`, `hee3 chain …` | integrations/bash (runs habitat-engine as producer) | `hee3:873-900` |
| `deploy/install-release --commit … --bundle … --deadline …` / `--control` | deploy | `install-release:6-8` |

## 4 HTTP (loopback only): the ollama API
| Endpoint | Use | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/` base | worker::native, via the pinned `/usr/bin/curl` (native.toml client pin) | `native.rs:413`; curl pin `native_provider.rs:505` |
| `GET version`, `GET tags`, `GET ps` | identity readback (model manifest, resident model) | `native.rs:1364,1374,1425` |
| `POST generate` | the model call (one per exchange) | `native.rs:1328-1331` |
| daemon identity | the LISTEN holder of :11434 from /proc/net/tcp{,6} + fd scan (N6b) | `native.rs` endpoint_holder |
No TCP listener exists in src (`TcpListener` appears only in tests).

